The caution, first: until a member is shown, every law and field that has PIN as an item or NoColl in its promise may be true and empty at the real protocol, and counts as closing nothing. row30 is such a law. Nothing false is proved by it. The promise's parts that read no pin (the book-keeping; Free₃ but for «record» and «shown») are not touched by that doubt.
Is it empty here? No record, reading and witness are shown at which the premises of row30 hold together. What is known, each by evaluation, not by a theorem (made-up weights; both stored key files): the last chain's start says yes at the two honest ends, over other base files than this library's · that K14's second part says yes on an honest key file over this library's base files is shown by no run: over other base files one run walked all five borders, and another the proof file's last chain.



The headline. row30: from (1) the promise in front: onAt … (shapeB₃ … 0) (Free₃ … 0) (open₃ 0) (z, s) y · (2) what the block has laid: Laid S s s' b yO G dot · (3) what is taken from others: NotOurs …:
