(2) is ours. Laid (Johnson/Desc/Third/Law/LaidDef.lean) is a structure of twenty-five facts on the two records. The block's yes gives it: laid_k14Second (Johnson/Desc/Third/Law/Laid.lean, over the base's own Third/K14BatchLinearConstraintsSecondPart.lean; from says_k14Second · sharp_k14Second · bookSays_k14Second · linDotRow_plain · dotIn_k14Second · inOrder_k14Second · alone_k14Second). At the key file's own description: laid_at_desc (Johnson/RunOne/KeyBridges23.lean): block number 0 of its last chain. This file imports the structure alone, none of these laws.

(3) NotOurs, five fields, whose each is:
